# Tangerine Compiler — Proof-Carrying Patch (audit §37)
# Self-hosting compiler written in Tangerine
#
# proof_patch.tg assembles ONE audit §37 ProofCarryingPatch report from the
# §31 SemanticDelta (semantic_delta.tg) / §36 ChangeBudget (change_budget.tg)
# machinery: the report bundles the delta itself with the four
# compiler-verified stage flags, the delta's domain row lists (§31 records),
# the §36-rule unsafe-marker rows, the abi / public-api deltas, two
# extensible surfaces (affected tests, uncovered new paths) and the budget
# envelope's violation list. The module reads ONLY SemanticDelta /
# ChangeBudget / VerifiedCompilationEvidence records (never AST / typed /
# MIR state) and mirrors the semantic_delta.tg / change_budget.tg /
# repair_candidates.tg idioms.
#
# CLAIM DISCIPLINE — what "proven" means here. The audit is explicit: "Do
# not call arbitrary application behavior 'proven' — this covers only what
# the compiler/verifiers actually established." A ProofCarryingPatch carries
# (1) a semantic_delta (what the §31 diff recorded between two snapshots),
# (2) a budget_result (what the §36 envelope check decided) and (3) the
# compiler-verified flags parses / resolves / types / ownership — and
# nothing else is ever claimed "proven". In particular:
#   - The four flags reflect the compiler PIPELINE stages only: parses = the
#     source parsed; resolves = name resolution succeeded; types = type
#     checking succeeded; ownership = the access/ownership convention checks
#     succeeded — each for the programs the patch spans. The flags are never
#     inferred here from a delta: every true flag of a patch comes from a
#     VerifiedCompilationEvidence (audit item 20 — the record of the stages
#     a REAL compile ran, assembled by the caller that RAN the stage; an
#     unset flag is an unproven property, never a denied one). The two
#     assemblers map the evidence flags onto the patch's four: parse_ok ->
#     parses, resolution_ok -> resolves, type_ok -> types, and
#     access_ok + resource_ok + mir_verify_ok -> ownership (the ownership
#     flag stands for the whole access/ownership convention + MIR-verify
#     gate). Repair machinery (repair_candidates.tg) is advisory intent and
#     is not part of the record: a patch reports what the compiler
#     established, never what a repair suggests.
#   - The row lists and deltas report what the §31/§36 machinery established
#     (the TYPED row records of the delta domain — audit item 14). No row
#     is invented: the flat lists are projections of existing delta rows,
#     and a surface the delta cannot see stays empty (documented gaps
#     below).
#   - Application behavior (what the patched program DOES at run time) is
#     never a patch's claim. A verified budget says the change fits its
#     allowance envelope; it does not say the change is behaviorally
#     correct.
#
# RECORD-NAME MAPPING (the audit's names onto the §31 records that exist —
# the §29 adaptation discipline, never invented look-alikes):
#   - The audit's EffectDelta / CapabilityDelta rows are semantic_delta.tg's
#     typed records: effect rows are EffectDelta { function, before: and
#     after: EffectSummaryView } (the §11 dirty word + capability-id texts
#     of both sides); capability rows are CapabilityDelta { function,
#     capability, before/after presence }. effect_delta / capability_delta
#     hold those records whole.
#   - ContractDelta / ApiDelta / AbiDelta exist under the audit's names:
#     ContractDelta rows carry the clause's StableContractId stable key
#     with the before/after ContractSemantic projections; ApiDelta /
#     AbiDelta (the changed flag + symmetric-difference rows) are REBUILT
#     from the delta's typed AbiDeltaView surfaces in proof_patch_of_delta
#     (semantic_delta.tg's public_api_delta / abi_delta fields carry the
#     full before/after row views; the patch's §37 report shape keeps the
#     changed-flag + rows form).
#   - unsafe_delta holds TEXT rows (the §36 counting rule's marker rows —
#     the audit's marker vocabulary), derived from the delta's TYPED
#     UnsafeFact rows (audit item 16): every CREATED fact of
#     delta.unsafe_delta renders as "<function> <kind-word>[:<site>]"
#     (semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text — the snapshot marker vocabulary
#     "unsafe-fn" / "extern-call:<name>" / "transmute" /
#     "unknown-call:<name>"). The ownership-row counting rule is gone.
#   - affected_tests / uncovered_new_paths are Vec[String] extension
#     surfaces the audit names but SemanticDelta carries no test or coverage
#     rows for (tests/coverage carry no rows today — documented in
#     semantic_delta.tg): they stay empty here, and a consumer holding
#     the semantic-index test relationships (semantic_index.tg) or the
#     coverage machinery fills them. The module never synthesizes a test or
#     a path name from an affected key.
#
# FLAT-LIST DERIVATION (proof_patch_of_delta, over ONE delta + ONE budget +
# ONE evidence record — the module doc's numbered checks):
#   1. contract_delta := the delta's contract rows (§31 ContractDelta).
#   2. effect_delta := the delta's effect rows (§31 EffectDelta — the
#      before/after §11 views).
#   3. capability_delta := the delta's capability rows (§31 CapabilityDelta
#      — presence before/after).
#   4. unsafe_delta := the marker rows of the §36 EXACT COUNTING RULE
#      (change_budget.tg check 7 — audit item 16): the CREATED facts of
#      delta.unsafe_delta rendered as "<function> <kind-word>[:<site>]"
#      (semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text), in the delta's own sorted row
#      order.
#   5. abi_delta / public_api_delta := rebuilt from the delta's typed
#      AbiDeltaView surfaces: the changed flag = the before/after row sets
#      differ (semantic_delta_rows_same), the rows = their symmetric
#      difference (semantic_delta_rows_diff).
#   6. budget_result := budget_verify(budget, delta) — the "budget:"
#      violation lines; empty = the delta verifies within the budget
#      envelope. That is the ONLY "budget verified" claim the patch makes.
#   7. The stage flags := the evidence mapping of the ONE evidence record
#      (see CLAIM DISCIPLINE); affected_tests / uncovered_new_paths stay
#      empty (see the mapping gaps above).
#
# SPAN FORM (proof_patch_between — the CHANGE patch, over the OLD and NEW
# evidence records of the two compilations a change spans): the flags are
# the SAME evidence mapping ANDed across BOTH records — parses :=
# old.parse_ok && new.parse_ok (and so on for resolves / types / ownership,
# ownership over the three evidence flags of each side). A stage property
# is claimed only when BOTH compilations the patch spans established it
# (one unverified endpoint leaves the property unproven for the span —
# claim discipline). The optional old_delta is the §31 diff the caller
# computed between the two compilations' finalized states (semantic_delta_of
# over their sessions' snapshots); when it is NOT supplied the report's
# delta stays the empty delta (which verifies against ANY budget) with the
# flags still set from the evidence, and the caller fills the real delta by
# re-running proof_patch_of_delta with it (the flags then ride the same
# evidence-driven mapping). The between-form never fabricates a delta.
#
# EMPTY-DEFAULT: proof_patch_new() is the claim-nothing patch — the empty
# §31 delta (which verifies against ANY budget: an empty delta carries no
# keys, no rows and no counts), every flag false, every list empty. All Vec
# fields are defaulted so a patch can be assembled incrementally: rows push
# onto the lists and flags are set as the pipeline stages establish them.
# Re-running proof_patch_of_delta over the patch's semantic_delta re-derives
# the report lists from a delta + budget and sets the flags from the
# evidence record the caller supplies.
#
# ANCHORS:
#   ProofCarryingPatch        — the §37 protocol record (the audit's struct,
#                               field for field).
#   VerifiedCompilationEvidence — audit item 20's record of what ONE real
#                               compilation's pipeline stages established
#                               (revision + the ten stage flags).
#   verified_compilation_evidence — the ONE documented constructor of the
#                               evidence record (revision + ten named stage
#                               flags, each documented below).
#   evidence_all_ok           — the predicate: every stage flag is true.
#   proof_patch_new           — the empty / claim-nothing patch.
#   proof_patch_of_delta      — the assembly convenience (delta + budget +
#                               evidence -> report; the derivation steps
#                               1-7 above; flags from the ONE evidence).
#   proof_patch_between       — the SPAN assembly (old + new evidence +
#                               budget + optional §31 delta -> report;
#                               flags ANDed across both evidence records).
#   proof_patch_proven_fields — the true-flag name list (the claim surface:
#                               parses / resolves / types / ownership only,
#                               fixed pipeline order).
#   unsafe markers            — "<function> <kind-word>[:<site>]" fact row
#                               texts (the §36 counting rule's rows).

use tg_compiler::semantic_delta::{
  SemanticDelta, ContractDelta, EffectDelta, CapabilityDelta, ApiDelta, AbiDelta,
  semantic_delta_empty, semantic_delta_rows_same, semantic_delta_rows_diff,
  semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text
}
use tg_compiler::change_budget::{ChangeBudget, budget_verify}

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The §37 protocol record
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# ONE §37 report: the §31 delta carried whole, the compiler-verified stage
# flags, the delta's domain row lists, the abi / public-api deltas, the two
# extensible surfaces and the §36 budget verdict. Every Vec field is
# defaulted so the patch can be assembled incrementally (see the module
# doc); semantic_delta / abi_delta / public_api_delta have no default and
# must be named on construction (proof_patch_new supplies the empty forms).
struct ProofCarryingPatch
  # The §31 semantic delta itself — the diff this patch reports.
  semantic_delta: SemanticDelta
  # The compiler-verified stage flags (pipeline stages only — see CLAIM
  # DISCIPLINE; false = unproven, never a denial).
  parses: Bool = false
  resolves: Bool = false
  types: Bool = false
  ownership: Bool = false
  # The delta's contract rows (§31 ContractDelta — before/after semantic
  # projections under the clause's StableContractId).
  contract_delta: Vec[ContractDelta] = Vec::new()
  # The delta's effect rows (§31 EffectDelta — before/after §11 views).
  effect_delta: Vec[EffectDelta] = Vec::new()
  # The delta's capability rows (§31 CapabilityDelta — before/after
  # presence).
  capability_delta: Vec[CapabilityDelta] = Vec::new()
  # The §36-rule unsafe-marker rows ("<function> <kind-word>[:<site>]" —
  # the created UnsafeFact rows of delta.unsafe_delta; the module doc's
  # derivation step 4).
  unsafe_delta: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # The ABI surface delta (changed flag + symmetric-difference rows —
  # rebuilt from the delta's typed AbiDeltaView surface).
  abi_delta: AbiDelta
  # The public-API surface delta (rebuilt the same way).
  public_api_delta: ApiDelta
  # The tests the patch affects — an extension surface (no §31 test rows
  # today; a consumer holding the index/test relationships fills it).
  affected_tests: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # The newly uncovered paths — an extension surface (no §31 coverage rows
  # today; a consumer holding the coverage machinery fills it).
  uncovered_new_paths: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  # The §36 envelope verdict: budget_verify(budget, delta)'s output lines
  # (empty = the delta verifies within the budget).
  budget_result: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
end

# The empty / claim-nothing patch: the empty §31 delta (which verifies
# against ANY budget), every stage flag false, no rows, no violations.
# proof_patch_proven_fields over it is empty — nothing is claimed.
pub def proof_patch_new() -> ProofCarryingPatch
  ProofCarryingPatch {
    semantic_delta: semantic_delta_empty(),
    parses: false,
    resolves: false,
    types: false,
    ownership: false,
    abi_delta: AbiDelta {
      abi_changed: false
    },
    public_api_delta: ApiDelta {
      public_api_changed: false
    }
  }
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The verification-evidence record (audit item 20)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# ONE VerifiedCompilationEvidence records what ONE REAL compilation's
# pipeline stages established — the evidence the patch flags come from
# (see CLAIM DISCIPLINE). revision is the content-addressed revision text
# of the program the evidence covers (the revision render of its
# finalized state — semantic_digest_render's "hi-lo" text of the final
# snapshot's digest; "" = not yet bound). The ten stage flags default
# false and have NO other sanctioned constructor: verified_compilation_
# evidence is the ONE public assembly path, and every flag is set only by
# naming it there with the stage meaning the constructor documents — a
# record literal can never claim a stage (an unset flag is an unproven
# property, never a denied one). The stage vocabulary, in pipeline order:
#   parse_ok             — the source parsed (lexer + parser success).
#   resolution_ok        — name resolution succeeded over the parsed tree.
#   type_ok              — type checking succeeded (the typed program is
#                          the type checker's output).
#   access_ok            — the access/ownership convention checker found
#                          no violations (access_check.tg).
#   resource_ok          — the resource checker found no violations
#                          (resource_check.tg).
#   mir_verify_ok        — the MIR verifier accepted the lowered program
#                          (verify_mir at the lowering boundary).
#   mono_verify_ok       — monomorphization completed and its verification
#                          checkpoint passed (the verifier over the
#                          monomorphized program).
#   post_opt_mir_verify_ok — the MIR verifier accepted the OPTIMIZED
#                          program (the final boundary before codegen).
#   effect_verify_ok     — the §11 effect-class annotation check passed
#                          over the lowered MIR
#                          (check_effect_class_annotations_mir).
#   abi_verify_ok        — the ABI/export surface check passed (the
#                          pub/extern surface the abi machinery audits).
# The evidence record itself makes no patch claim: the ASSEMBLERS below
# map the flags onto the patch's four (parse_ok -> parses, resolution_ok
# -> resolves, type_ok -> types, access_ok + resource_ok + mir_verify_ok
# -> ownership). mono_verify_ok / post_opt_mir_verify_ok /
# effect_verify_ok / abi_verify_ok have no patch-flag counterpart — they
# ride the record for the evidence_all_ok gate and for consumers that
# hold a real pipeline.
struct VerifiedCompilationEvidence
  # The revision text of the program this evidence covers ("" = not yet
  # bound).
  revision: String = ""
  # parse_ok: the source parsed (lexer + parser success).
  parse_ok: Bool = false
  # resolution_ok: name resolution succeeded over the parsed tree.
  resolution_ok: Bool = false
  # type_ok: type checking succeeded.
  type_ok: Bool = false
  # access_ok: the access/ownership convention checker found no
  # violations.
  access_ok: Bool = false
  # resource_ok: the resource checker found no violations.
  resource_ok: Bool = false
  # mir_verify_ok: the MIR verifier accepted the lowered program.
  mir_verify_ok: Bool = false
  # mono_verify_ok: monomorphization completed and its verification
  # checkpoint passed.
  mono_verify_ok: Bool = false
  # post_opt_mir_verify_ok: the MIR verifier accepted the optimized
  # program (the final boundary before codegen).
  post_opt_mir_verify_ok: Bool = false
  # effect_verify_ok: the §11 effect-class annotation check passed over
  # the lowered MIR.
  effect_verify_ok: Bool = false
  # abi_verify_ok: the ABI/export surface check passed.
  abi_verify_ok: Bool = false
end

# The ONE documented constructor of a VerifiedCompilationEvidence (see the
# record doc for the stage meanings). revision is the content-addressed
# revision text of the program the stages verified; every flag is a named
# parameter whose meaning the record doc states — a caller sets a flag
# true ONLY for a stage the compiler actually ran to success, and sets the
# flags in the pipeline order below. The record is otherwise claim-nothing:
# every flag the caller does not name stays false.
pub def verified_compilation_evidence(
  revision: String,
  parse: Bool,
  resolution: Bool,
  types: Bool,
  access: Bool,
  resource: Bool,
  mir: Bool,
  mono: Bool,
  post_opt: Bool,
  effects: Bool,
  abi: Bool
) -> VerifiedCompilationEvidence
  VerifiedCompilationEvidence {
    revision: revision,
    parse_ok: parse,
    resolution_ok: resolution,
    type_ok: types,
    access_ok: access,
    resource_ok: resource,
    mir_verify_ok: mir,
    mono_verify_ok: mono,
    post_opt_mir_verify_ok: post_opt,
    effect_verify_ok: effects,
    abi_verify_ok: abi
  }
end

# The evidence_all_ok predicate: every one of the ten stage flags is true
# — the evidence describes a compilation that ran the WHOLE documented
# pipeline to success (parse through the abi surface). Any false flag
# means the corresponding stage property is unproven (never denied).
pub def evidence_all_ok(evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence) -> Bool
  evidence.parse_ok && evidence.resolution_ok && evidence.type_ok &&
    evidence.access_ok && evidence.resource_ok && evidence.mir_verify_ok &&
    evidence.mono_verify_ok && evidence.post_opt_mir_verify_ok &&
    evidence.effect_verify_ok && evidence.abi_verify_ok
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# THE ASSEMBLY — ONE ProofCarryingPatch from ONE delta + ONE budget
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The shared derived-row record: the report's §31 flat lists + the abi /
# public-api rebuilt records + the §36 budget verdict, derived from ONE
# delta + ONE budget (the module doc's numbered steps 1-6). The two
# assemblers (proof_patch_of_delta / proof_patch_between) differ only in
# the stage-flag derivation (step 7); the rows are always the same
# function of the delta.
struct ProofCarryingPatchRows
  contract_delta: Vec[ContractDelta] = Vec::new()
  effect_delta: Vec[EffectDelta] = Vec::new()
  capability_delta: Vec[CapabilityDelta] = Vec::new()
  unsafe_delta: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  abi_delta: AbiDelta
  public_api_delta: ApiDelta
  budget_result: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
end

def proof_patch_rows_of(budget: ChangeBudget, delta: SemanticDelta) -> ProofCarryingPatchRows
  let violations = budget_verify(&budget, &delta)
  let contract_rows = delta.contract_delta.clone()
  let effect_rows = delta.effect_delta.clone()
  let capability_rows = delta.capability_delta.clone()
  let unsafe_rows = proof_unsafe_rows(&delta)
  let api_changed = !semantic_delta_rows_same(&delta.public_api_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.public_api_delta.after.rows)
  let api_rows = semantic_delta_rows_diff(&delta.public_api_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.public_api_delta.after.rows)
  let abi_changed = !semantic_delta_rows_same(&delta.abi_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.abi_delta.after.rows)
  let abi_rows = semantic_delta_rows_diff(&delta.abi_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.abi_delta.after.rows)
  ProofCarryingPatchRows {
    contract_delta: contract_rows,
    effect_delta: effect_rows,
    capability_delta: capability_rows,
    unsafe_delta: unsafe_rows,
    abi_delta: AbiDelta {
      abi_changed: abi_changed,
      abi_rows: abi_rows
    },
    public_api_delta: ApiDelta {
      public_api_changed: api_changed,
      public_api_rows: api_rows
    },
    budget_result: violations
  }
end

# The evidence mapping of ONE stage group (see CLAIM DISCIPLINE): the
# ownership flag stands for the WHOLE access/ownership gate — the access
# convention check AND the resource check AND the MIR verification of the
# lowered program — so it is the AND of the three evidence flags.
def proof_evidence_parses(evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence) -> Bool
  evidence.parse_ok
end

def proof_evidence_resolves(evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence) -> Bool
  evidence.resolution_ok
end

def proof_evidence_types(evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence) -> Bool
  evidence.type_ok
end

def proof_evidence_ownership(evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence) -> Bool
  evidence.access_ok && evidence.resource_ok && evidence.mir_verify_ok
end

# Assembles ONE report over ONE §31 delta + ONE budget + ONE evidence
# record: derives the report's flat lists from the delta (the module doc's
# steps 1-5), runs the §36 envelope (step 6) and sets the four stage flags
# from the evidence (step 7 — the evidence mapping above). Nothing a delta
# alone carries can prove that a pipeline stage ran; the evidence record
# is the only flag source (see CLAIM DISCIPLINE).
pub def proof_patch_of_delta(
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  delta: SemanticDelta,
  evidence: VerifiedCompilationEvidence
) -> ProofCarryingPatch
  let rows = proof_patch_rows_of(&budget, &delta)
  ProofCarryingPatch {
    semantic_delta: delta,
    parses: proof_evidence_parses(&evidence),
    resolves: proof_evidence_resolves(&evidence),
    types: proof_evidence_types(&evidence),
    ownership: proof_evidence_ownership(&evidence),
    contract_delta: rows.contract_delta.clone(),
    effect_delta: rows.effect_delta.clone(),
    capability_delta: rows.capability_delta.clone(),
    unsafe_delta: rows.unsafe_delta.clone(),
    abi_delta: rows.abi_delta.clone(),
    public_api_delta: rows.public_api_delta.clone(),
    budget_result: rows.budget_result.clone()
  }
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# THE SPAN ASSEMBLY — ONE ProofCarryingPatch between two compilations
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# proof_patch_between assembles the CHANGE patch over the OLD and NEW
# evidence records of the two compilations a change spans. The stage
# flags are the evidence mapping ANDed across BOTH records: parses :=
# old.parse_ok && new.parse_ok, resolves := old.resolution_ok &&
# new.resolution_ok, types := old.type_ok && new.type_ok, ownership :=
# the ownership group of the old side AND the ownership group of the new
# side. A stage property is claimed only when BOTH compilations the patch
# spans established it — one unverified endpoint leaves the property
# unproven for the span (claim discipline). old_delta, when supplied, is
# the §31 diff the caller computed between the two compilations'
# finalized states (semantic_delta_of over the sessions' snapshots — the
# delta computed from real evidence); the report rows + budget verdict
# derive from it (the module doc's steps 1-6). When it is NOT supplied
# the report's delta stays the empty delta (which verifies against ANY
# budget), the flags still come from the evidence, and the caller fills
# the real delta by re-running proof_patch_of_delta with it — the
# between-form never fabricates a delta.
pub def proof_patch_between(
  old: VerifiedCompilationEvidence,
  new: VerifiedCompilationEvidence,
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  old_delta: Option[SemanticDelta]
) -> ProofCarryingPatch
  let delta = match old_delta
  when Option::Some(d) then d
  when Option::None then semantic_delta_empty()
  end
  let rows = proof_patch_rows_of(&budget, &delta)
  ProofCarryingPatch {
    semantic_delta: delta,
    parses: old.parse_ok && new.parse_ok,
    resolves: old.resolution_ok && new.resolution_ok,
    types: old.type_ok && new.type_ok,
    ownership: proof_evidence_ownership(&old) && proof_evidence_ownership(&new),
    contract_delta: rows.contract_delta.clone(),
    effect_delta: rows.effect_delta.clone(),
    capability_delta: rows.capability_delta.clone(),
    unsafe_delta: rows.unsafe_delta.clone(),
    abi_delta: rows.abi_delta.clone(),
    public_api_delta: rows.public_api_delta.clone(),
    budget_result: rows.budget_result.clone()
  }
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The §36-rule unsafe-marker rows
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The rows of change_budget.tg's EXACT COUNTING RULE (check 7 — audit item
# 16): the CREATED UnsafeFact rows of the delta's unsafe_delta, rendered in
# the marker vocabulary (semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text) in the delta's
# own (sorted) row order. The ownership/effect-row sources of the former
# rule never participate.
def proof_unsafe_rows(delta: SemanticDelta) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for fact in delta.unsafe_delta.created do
    out.push(semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text(&fact))
  end
  out
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The claim surface — the proven-field name list
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The names of the stage flags that are TRUE, in the fixed pipeline order
# (parses, resolves, types, ownership). These four reflect the compiler
# pipeline stages ONLY (see the module doc); an empty list means no stage
# property is claimed — the fail-closed claim surface, never a denial of a
# property the pipeline actually established.
pub def proof_patch_proven_fields(patch: ProofCarryingPatch) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  if patch.parses then
    out.push("parses")
  end
  if patch.resolves then
    out.push("resolves")
  end
  if patch.types then
    out.push("types")
  end
  if patch.ownership then
    out.push("ownership")
  end
  out
end
